# Web UI / UX — design system first

## Controls

- **Do not** use bare `<input>`, `<select>`, `<textarea>`, or `<button>` in `web/src/pages/`, `web/src/components/` (except inside `web/src/components/ui/` primitives).
- **Do** use themed primitives from `@/components/ui/`: `Button`, `Input`, `Select` (Radix), `Checkbox` (Radix), `Dialog` (Radix), `Tabs` (Radix), `Label` (Radix), `IconButton`, plus `Card`, `Badge`, and layout (`AppShell`, `TopBar`).
- **Headless UI**: implement interactive controls with **Radix UI** primitives (`@radix-ui/react-*`) inside `components/ui/` — not native `<select>`, `<dialog>`, or hand-rolled tabs/checkboxes on pages.
- **New patterns** (e.g. textarea, radio, dropdown menu): add a Radix-based component under `web/src/components/ui/` with the same borders, radius, blue focus ring, and dark mode tokens as `Input` / `Button` — then consume it from pages.

## Allowed native / platform elements

- Structure and navigation: `<main>`, headings, `<Link>`, `<NavLink>`, `<dialog>`, lists, tables.
- Primitives **inside** `components/ui/*` may render native elements as the implementation detail.

## Styling

- Prefer `className` + `cn()` on primitives for one-off layout (e.g. `pl-9` with a search icon). Avoid copy-pasting full field Tailwind strings onto pages.

## Rationale

Keeps EPIC-12 and future UI aligned with one visual system (blue accent, neutral palette, rounded-xl) and consistent accessibility/focus behavior via Radix.

## Regression guard

- `Button` must render `{children}` inside the native `<button>` (never a self-closing `<button />` without children).
- Add or extend `src/**/*.test.tsx` when changing primitives so labels stay visible (`getByRole` / `toHaveTextContent`).
